Subject: [PATCH 02/14] fix(gui): retry rate-limit and mid-stream disconnects
 without duplicating messages

- streamThunkWrapper now also retries on 429/rate-limit/quota errors and
  mid-stream disconnects (Premature Close, socket hang up, ECONNRESET),
  which typically occur when an overloaded LLM server stalls and the
  connection is dropped; 4 attempts with 2/4/8/16s backoff
- streamResponse and streamResponseAfterToolCall no longer put their
  history mutations inside the retried closure: preparation runs once, so
  a retry continues the turn (partial assistant content is kept as an
  assistant prefill and merged back into the same message by streamUpdate)
  instead of duplicating the user/tool messages and regenerating from
  scratch - this is what made a manual "continue" re-run all the thinking
- preparation failures still open the StreamError dialog (exported
  showStreamErrorDialog helper, typed with AppThunkDispatch)
