From 74660854fc473d7ea7f1754ee7c627729f3dab27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sam <sam@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:36:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] fix(llm): keep reasoning when a delta carries both
 reasoning and content

Some OpenAI-compatible servers emit reasoning_content and answer text in
the same delta (typically the final chunk of a reasoning turn); the
previous single-message conversion silently dropped the reasoning.

- new fromChatCompletionChunkAll returns every message carried by the
  delta, reasoning first
- _streamChat consumes it so both messages are yielded in order
- fromChatCompletionChunk delegates and keeps its old first-message
  semantics for the remaining call sites (WatsonX, LLM base class)
- unit tests for the dual, reasoning-only and tool-call cases
